{
  "name": "city-downtown-cascade",
  "description": "Drive the whole downtown to collapse: cut supports at the base of every block in turn, then a second pass working the piles, then a settle window. Scale-ceiling test -- it exists to measure the ceiling and to prove the city still settles and stays uncorrupted there, not to pass the standard gates. Measured on a cuda-stress build: peaks at ~2,300 bodies and ~7,700 broken bonds, fully settles (awake returns to 0), 0 corrupt island bodies, 0 membership violations, server tick p95 peak ~36 ms against a 16.7 ms budget. Note it PLATEAUS: doubling the fire moved broken bonds only 7,405 -> 7,693. A hand-played session on a CPU-stress build reached 26,288 bonds and 7,254 bodies, which is roughly 3x this -- the difference is solver residual on the unconverged CPU path, not extra physics. Run this against both builds if you need that comparison.",
  "symptom": [
    "scale",
    "cascade",
    "overload"
  ],
  "path": "/city?portal=true",
  "matchId": "city-downtown-cascade-{iter}",
  "durationMs": 337500,
  "join": "auto",
  "serverEnv": {
    "VIBE_PHYSICS_BACKEND": "physx_gpu",
    "WT_STRICT_SNAPSHOT_DATAGRAMS": "1",
    "VIBE_CITY_SCENE": "fractured-downtown.json",
    "VIBE_CITY_GRID": "1",
    "VIBE_CITY_VARIED_HEIGHTS": "0",
    "VIBE_CITY_STRESS_LIMIT_SCALE": "1.0"
